(32, 184, 'Child Victims: Describe shelter options available specifically for child trafficking victims, including non-specialized shelters, such as homeless shelters, group homes, migrant shelters, or juvenile justice detention centers. Indicate what kind of specialized care child victims received in these shelters, and if children had a choice among shelter options or could leave shelters to attend school. Which entity determined whether a child trafficking victim was placed into a shelter, returned to their family, or placed in another arrangement such as with a foster family, and did these authorities receive training on trafficking and the vulnerabilities of child trauma survivors? Indicate if authorities returned child victims to live with family members who may have been involved in their exploitation or how authorities prevented children from returning to situations of exploitation.', '2026-08-25 05:12:57', '2026-08-25 05:12:57'),
